"""Write the source classification, extraction and bounded capability record."""
import hashlib,importlib.util,json,re
from pathlib import Path
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[2]
spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('g',HERE.with_suffix('.py'));g=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(g)
def write(name,v):(HERE/name).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\n')
rows=[];plots=[];excluded=[]
for mid,q in sorted(g.SOURCE_BY_ID.items()):
 level=q[':question/difficulty'][':db/ident'].split('/')[-1];f=q[':question/answer-fields'][0]
 rows.append(f"| {mid} | {q[':db/id']} | {level} | radio / selection | {mid} | source-bank:{mid} | none (unchanged path) | {'excluded: singular field on path' if mid in g.EXCLUDED else 'supported'} |")
 path=re.search(r'!\[\]\((.*?)\)',q[':question/problem'])[1];p=Path('/media/jake/SSD/EDB/math')/path;digest=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest();assert p.stem==digest
 plots.append({'source':mid,'path':path,'sha256':digest,'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'placement':'prompt before integral','visual_role':'Cartesian axes, labeled intercepts/endpoints, blue path C and direction arrows','inspection':'Inspected /tmp/line-contact.png; path geometry and traversal agree with text and parametrization','reuse':'unchanged; multiplier affects scalar field only','new_plot_rating':'none'})
 if mid in g.EXCLUDED:excluded.append({'source':mid,'db_id':q[':db/id'],'level':level,'reason':g.EXCLUDED[mid],'source_prompt':q[':question/problem'],'source_solution':q[':question/worked-solution'],'profile':'source-bank:'+mid,'complete_observed_bank':[{'source_field':f[':answer-field/id'],'source_answer':a[':answer/id'],'exact_value':a[':answer/value'],'correct':a[':answer/id']==f[':answer-field/correct'][':answer/id'],'unimplemented_candidate_recipe':'c * ('+g.clean(a[':answer/value'])+')','recipe_status':'not validated or served for this excluded template'} for a in f[':answer-field/choices']]})
(HERE/'classification.md').write_text(f"# Classification: Evaluating Line Integrals With Respect to X and Y\n\nCaptured EDB basis {g.CAPTURE['basis']}, lineage `{g.CAPTURE['lineage']}`. The current bank contains 12 practice questions (9 moderate, 3 hard), all single-field five-choice radio questions. Canonical e-9521 is evidence only and never inventory. No easy practice source was observed.\n\nEach distinct integrand structure and solution operation sequence is retained as its own template, with its own complete observed five-option bank. Numeric scaling creates variants within a template. The bounded generator supports five smooth moderate templates and all three hard templates; four rational templates require an explicit improper-integral interpretation and are excluded.\n\n| Source | Entity | Level | Field | Template | Bank profile | New plots | Status |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n"+'\n'.join(rows)+"\n\nThe plots are central geometric evidence in the sources, but all supported variations reuse the path unchanged and therefore need no new plot. All 13 source/canonical diagrams were inspected together. Source differences are retained in source.json and source-components.json; excluded templates are detailed in excluded-sources.json.\n\nSource corrections are local to new generated instances: q-124120's general formula incorrectly labels dy while its derivative and requested integral use dx; q-124217 and q-124278 label the evaluated LHS dx while the prompt and all calculations use dy. These original records remain unchanged and do not count toward this package's fully validated reserve.\n")
(HERE/'template-extraction.md').write_text("# Template extraction\n\nThe supplied object is a scalar field f(x,y), an oriented path C, and one requested coordinate differential dx or dy. The response is one exact scalar integral, selected from a field-owned five-choice bank under key selection. Every source is described and mapped in source-components.json or excluded-sources.json, including all choices, source fields, full prompt, and full worked solution. No distractor interpretation is asserted without evidence.\n\nThe fixed backbone is: state the coordinate line-integral formula; rewrite ellipse semiaxes when present; parameterize the supplied path with its traversal bounds; compute the requested coordinate derivative; substitute the field; evaluate the integral. Hard templates retain the observed u=cos(t) or u=cos²(t) substitution stage and its complete endpoint calculation. Moderate polynomial, square-root and trig stages remain distinct. Repeated instructional sentences and all source equation stages are preserved. Documented differential-label errors and captured TeX artifacts are corrected in new records only.\n\nThe sole variable slot is the positive constant c multiplying the entire original integrand. Observed c=1 replays sources for evidence; sampling is the explicitly narrower domain c in {2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9}. Positive nonzero scaling preserves the real domain, smoothness along the path, all integration/substitution stages, and source difficulty. Correct answers are computed first using exact SymPy integration. Each original bank profile is scaled as a whole: every source option v becomes c·v, with the same correct designation. These are conservative exact observed-value recipes; no inferred feedback is added. Zero/negative scales and changes of path, orientation, differential, powers, or integrand structure are outside this version.\n\nThe path is deliberately fixed in this bounded package: changing it would affect endpoint values, branch behavior, diagram and in some cases integration method. Diagram labels and target coordinate remain fixed and validated; there is no declared variable target slot. A changed-c case with the entire path held fixed checks all prompt, field-substitution, solution and bank dependencies. The finite sampling domain is exhaustively validated per template. Seeds select content from that domain; they do not create additional content.\n\nComplete source-bank replay, normalized prompt/solution fidelity, exact mathematical correctness, and actual grader results are reported separately. All printed scalar rows and integral evaluations are independently parsed from rendered TeX and checked against the displayed field and path. review.md shows every supported source next to c=2 and c=9 variants.\n")
(HERE/'plot-extraction.md').write_text("# Path plots\n\nSources place one image before the integral. Each has black x/y axes, numerical endpoint/intercept labels, a blue line/circular/elliptical arc labeled C, and blue traversal arrows. All text endpoints, arc sectors and directions agree with the source diagrams in the inspected contact sheet. Moderate line paths and hard semicircle/ellipse paths are retained exactly. Source aspect ratio is incidental to the line-integral calculation; endpoint geometry, arc selection and arrows are meaningful.\n\nOnly the scalar integrand changes. Reuse the existing content-addressed PNGs without alteration. No curve, endpoint, axis, numerical label, arrow, styling or placement is sampled. Thus the new-plot rating is none for every supported template. plot-assets.json records exact paths, SHA-256 bytes, and source placement. No new asset publication or plot renderer is needed.\n")
write('plot-assets.json',plots);write('excluded-sources.json',excluded)
write('capabilities.json',{'supported_levels':['moderate','hard'],'unsupported_levels':['easy'],'finite_limits':{'moderate':40,'hard':24},'finite_limit_scope':'new mathematical tasks before excluding existing, shown or reserved tasks; c=1 is replay-only','parameter_domain':{'c':list(g.SCALES)},'exceptions':[{'level':'easy','reason':'No easy source observed; promoting or demoting moderate/hard templates would lack evidence. This bounded package has no easy generator.','required_reserve':5,'produced':0,'filled':False}]+[{'source_id':mid,'reason':reason,'filled':False} for mid,reason in g.EXCLUDED.items()]})
write('source-corrections.json',[{'source':'q-124120','correction':'General formula LHS dy becomes dx; requested differential and actual derivative are dx.','source_unchanged':True},{'source':'q-124217','correction':'Evaluation LHS dx becomes dy; requested differential and actual derivative are dy.','source_unchanged':True},{'source':'q-124278','correction':'Evaluation LHS dx becomes dy; requested differential and actual derivative are dy.','source_unchanged':True}])
